    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0274" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg16"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1496</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-23T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1915, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 24, 9 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1672. Recent victory of Germans in East Prussia complete. Over 100,000 prisoners;
                    over 300 guns. Russians will probably have to abandon Warsaw. Much talk here of
                    separate peace with Russia. Bread cards now issued but convinced supplies enough
                    to last until next harvest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
